title Power Supply Conversion & Delivery Process

Power Source [color: gray] {
  Supply {
    Provide input energy [type: activity, icon: zap]
    Input available [type: event, icon: plug]
  }
}

Power Supply Unit [color: blue] {
  Input Stage {
    Receive input power [type: activity, icon: plug]
    Identify input type [type: activity, icon: search]
    AC or DC? [type: gateway, icon: x]
    Accept AC mains / grid [type: activity, icon: power]
    Accept DC source [type: activity, icon: battery]
  }
  Conversion {
    Select conversion method [type: gateway, icon: x]
    Linear path [type: activity, icon: trending-down]
    Transform (mains frequency) [type: activity, icon: refresh-cw]
    Rectify [type: activity, icon: activity]
    Filter (capacitors / pi) [type: activity, icon: filter]
    Linear regulate [type: activity, icon: sliders]
    Switched-mode path [type: activity, icon: cpu]
    Rectify & filter input [type: activity, icon: activity]
    High-frequency switching [type: activity, icon: repeat]
    High-freq transform / induct [type: activity, icon: refresh-cw]
    Rectify high-freq output [type: activity, icon: activity]
    Feedback regulate (duty cycle) [type: activity, icon: sliders]
  }
  Optional Functions {
    Apply protections? [type: gateway, icon: x]
    Current limiting / foldback [type: activity, icon: minus-circle]
    Fault protection (SCP/OCP/OVP/OTP) [type: activity, icon: shield]
    Power conditioning / noise filter [type: activity, icon: filter]
    Power factor correction [type: activity, icon: bar-chart]
    Energy storage / UPS backup [type: activity, icon: battery-charging]
  }
  Output Stage {
    Deliver regulated power [type: activity, icon: send]
    Output rails ready [type: event, icon: check-circle]
  }
}

Load [color: green] {
  Consumption {
    Receive power [type: activity, icon: zap]
    Draw current [type: activity, icon: activity]
    Load powered [type: event, icon: smile]
  }
}

// Source to Input
Provide input energy > Input available
Input available > Receive input power
Receive input power > Identify input type
Identify input type > AC or DC?
AC or DC? > Accept AC mains / grid : AC
AC or DC? > Accept DC source : DC
Accept AC mains / grid > Select conversion method
Accept DC source > Select conversion method

// Conversion paths
Select conversion method > Linear path : Linear
Select conversion method > Switched-mode path : Switching
Linear path > Transform (mains frequency)
Transform (mains frequency) > Rectify
Rectify > Filter (capacitors / pi)
Filter (capacitors / pi) > Linear regulate
Linear regulate > Apply protections?
Switched-mode path > Rectify & filter input
Rectify & filter input > High-frequency switching
High-frequency switching > High-freq transform / induct
High-freq transform / induct > Rectify high-freq output
Rectify high-freq output > Feedback regulate (duty cycle)
Feedback regulate (duty cycle) > Apply protections?

// Optional functions
Apply protections? > Current limiting / foldback : Yes
Apply protections? > Deliver regulated power : No
Current limiting / foldback > Fault protection (SCP/OCP/OVP/OTP)
Fault protection (SCP/OCP/OVP/OTP) > Power conditioning / noise filter
Power conditioning / noise filter > Power factor correction
Power factor correction > Energy storage / UPS backup
Energy storage / UPS backup > Deliver regulated power

// Output to Load
Deliver regulated power > Output rails ready
Output rails ready > Receive power
Receive power > Draw current
Draw current > Load powered
